usage: static_limit_response.py [-h] [--Lx LX] [--Ly LY] [--shear SHEAR]
                                [--Jx JX] [--Jy JY] [--Jz JZ] --lambda LAM
                                [--spring-k SPRING_K] [--starts STARTS]
                                [--seed SEED] [--parity {trial,unrestricted}]
                                --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR [--plot]

Relax every bond in the strict static limit and measure source response. Fixed
zero-flux, Wilson(+,+) matter sector; no phonon kinetic term. Unlike
static_vbs_response.py, the background is a finite-torus stationary
configuration of all bond variables, not a prescribed uniform BZ solution.
Multistart local minimization is not a global optimality certificate.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --Lx LX
  --Ly LY
  --shear SHEAR
  --Jx JX
  --Jy JY
  --Jz JZ
  --lambda LAM
  --spring-k SPRING_K
  --starts STARTS
  --seed SEED
  --parity {trial,unrestricted}
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --plot
